  <title>Serial numbers</title>

  <p><guiseq><gui>General</gui><gui>Serial numbers</gui></guiseq> lists every
  serial number: when it was made or received, which invoice sold it and to
  whom, and how many <gui>Events</gui> have been recorded against it, such as
  repairs or warranty claims.</p>

  <list>
    <item><p>Type into the <gui>Product</gui>, <gui>Serial number</gui> and
    <gui>Contact</gui> search boxes to find one. <gui>Refresh</gui> reloads
    the list.</p></item>
    <item><p>Double click a serial number to see its events.</p></item>
    <item><p>Right click it to <gui>Add event</gui>, open the <gui>Invoice
    hub</gui> of the invoice that sold it, or <gui>Select serial number</gui>
    to put it in the print box below.</p></item>
  </list>

  <section id="add">
  <title>Adding by hand</title>
  <p>Serial numbers are normally made when a product is manufactured or
  received. To add one that was missed, for instance so it can be sold on an
  invoice, choose <gui>Add serial number entry</gui> from the window menu.
  Choose the <gui>Product</gui>, type the <gui>Serial number</gui>, set the
  <gui>Date</gui> and click <gui>Add serial number</gui>. A number the product
  already has is refused.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="events">
  <title>Recording an event</title>
  <p>Choose <gui>Add serial number event</gui> from the window menu, or
  <gui>Add event</gui> from the right click menu. Choose the
  <gui>Contact</gui>, the <gui>Product</gui> and its <gui>Serial number</gui>,
  set the <gui>Date</gui>, describe what happened in <gui>Description</gui>
  and click <gui>Add event</gui>. Events also show on the contact's
  <gui>Warranty</gui> tab in <link xref="contact_history"/>.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="print">
  <title>Printing a label</title>
  <p>Choose the label <gui>Printer</gui> and <gui>Template</gui>, type or scan
  the <gui>Serial number</gui> and press <key>Enter</key>, or click
  <gui>Print serial number</gui>. <gui>Edit</gui> opens a Zebra template in
  the <link xref="zebra_designer"/>; it asks for the administrator
  password.</p>
  </section>

</page>
